{
  "$schema_version": 1,
  "$authority": "core/envelope.proto :: shared.proto.core.v1.ContentType",
  "$spec": "construct-docs/architecture/WIRE_FORMAT.md",
  "$decision": "construct-docs/decisions/wire-format-one-authority.md",
  "$purpose": [
    "Every client that speaks this protocol classifies a content type before it does anything",
    "with the payload: transcript or control, which handler, whether a sealed envelope may name",
    "it out loud. Until 2026-08-23 each client carried that classification in its own switch, and",
    "the two had already drifted — iOS treated {12,14,21,23,24,25,26} as control while the TUI",
    "treated {12,13,14,25,26} as silent, because the two lists were answering different questions",
    "nobody had written down. Divergence here does not fail loudly: a message renders as a bubble",
    "on one client and vanishes on the other, and it surfaces weeks later as 'the phone shows",
    "something the terminal does not'.",
    "This file is the answer, and every client must have a test that reads it. A new content type",
    "is added here in the same change as the proto; the client that has not learned it goes red."
  ],
  "$fields": {
    "value": "the enum number; the authority for it is envelope.proto, this file must not disagree",
    "name": "the enum name in envelope.proto",
    "knst_byte5": "may this value appear in KNST frame byte 5 (i.e. inside the ciphertext)",
    "disposition": "transcript_incoming | transcript_own_device | silent_control | not_carried",
    "routing_kind": "what a client's contentType -> routing-kind mapping must return",
    "session_control_op": "PING | READY | RESET_INIT | END | null — the SessionControl op it denotes",
    "framed_side_channel": "call_signal | delivery_receipt | contact_card | profile | null — handler for a framed payload",
    "sealed_inner_content_type": "may SealedInner.content_type carry this value (0 means absent)"
  },
  "$notes": {
    "disposition": [
      "silent_control — must NEVER reach the transcript. A bubble here is a user-visible defect;",
      "  __session_reset_notify__ spent four months writing itself into transcripts this way.",
      "transcript_own_device — belongs in the transcript as a SENT bubble, not an incoming one.",
      "not_carried — never framed by any current producer. A client that receives one has met a",
      "  peer it does not understand; it must not guess, and it must not crash."
    ],
    "sealed_inner_content_type": [
      "Only 0, 21 and 24 may appear. 0 is proto3 absence — the generic baseline. 21 is sent when",
      "the ratchet may be unusable, so it cannot ride inside it; 24 says 'archive the session you",
      "hold', and reading that from inside the ciphertext would require establishing the session",
      "that is being archived. Everything else moved into byte 5 precisely so the server stopped",
      "seeing it — putting one back on SealedInner undoes that, silently."
    ]
  },
